comments[15]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-14T07:11:28.225Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: searched all statuses for surface replication false-positive activation,trigger scope,unrelated file changes,and content-aware triggers. pm-kmnvug fixed shared non-trigger activation but does not address unrelated hunks inside an explicitly shared trigger file; no item tracks that distinct residual."
  "2026-08-14T07:18:30.525Z","harness:codex","TDD/quality evidence: the existing full pnpm quality:static chain reproduced false activation of annotation-mutation-receipts from an outputBudget-only hunk. New focused tests prove relevant diff markers activate, unrelated hunks stay inactive, missing diff evidence activates fail-closed, and malformed trigger objects are refused. The real changeset now reports zero unrelated active replication sets."
  "2026-08-14T07:55:45.881Z","harness:codex","Completion evidence: replication triggers accept changed_lines_contain_any, relevant diff markers activate every required-member ratchet, unrelated shared-file hunks do not, missing diff evidence activates fail-closed, malformed objects fail declaration validation, and a no-default-branch Git fixture is covered. Real changeset gate, linked 15-test suite, complete static chain, and exact coverage all pass."
  "2026-08-14T09:03:16.889Z","harness:codex","Review-closeout evidence: CodeRabbit identified deleted trigger paths as missing from the changed-file census. All three git diff filters now include D, and the focused regression deletes a structured trigger file, proves the replication set activates, and verifies the missing-member violation. The 15-test gate suite and full 115-test review set pass."
  "2026-08-14T09:31:39.837Z","harness:codex","Final gate evidence: the real surface-replication gate and its deleted-trigger negative control passed inside the exact 7,288-test coverage run; the complete lint/quality:static chain also passed with no active recurrence violations."
  "2026-08-14T10:02:44.145Z","harness:codex","Delivery closeout 2026-08-14: PR #1013 exact head cd6d04061 merged to main as a7f68fb84. Deleted-trigger coverage, fail-closed replication behavior, and real-changeset negative controls passed locally and in hosted CI. All review threads are resolved; the final CodeRabbit inspection found no actionable issue."
  "2026-08-14T12:11:41.132Z","harness:codex","Regression evidence 2026-08-14: the universal outputCursor addition changed only unrelated lines in src/sdk/cli-contracts/tool-schema.ts, but annotation-mutation-receipts still uses that shared registry as a whole-file trigger. pnpm quality:static therefore demanded artificial edits across every annotation transport. Reusing this canonical item because its content-scoped trigger acceptance and learning explicitly own this exact false-positive class."
  "2026-08-14T12:16:58.184Z","harness:codex","Focused evidence: annotation tool-schema activation is now content-scoped; an outputCursor-only hunk leaves the set inactive while a changed full marker still requires all annotation members. The 16-test suite and real changeset replication gate pass with no waiver or artificial edits."
  "2026-08-14T12:57:48.251Z","harness:codex","Final verification after live reopen: annotation replication triggers now inspect relevant added/removed hunk content rather than any shared-schema edit. The 16-test gate proves unrelated outputCursor lines stay inactive, annotation markers activate every required member, malformed declarations fail closed, and the real changeset gate passes."
  "2026-08-15T00:35:41.964Z","harness:codex","Continuation evidence 2026-08-15: adding the unrelated history-repair --normalize-provenance flag to the shared flag-contract registry still activates the annotation-mutation-receipts set because that remaining trigger is whole-file scoped. Reusing this canonical item again; the prior tool-schema fix established the exact semantic-trigger contract, and this pass closes the residual flag-contract gap without a waiver or artificial annotation edits."
  "2026-08-15T01:56:45.923Z","harness:codex","Delivery evidence 2026-08-15: surface replication activation now evaluates declared semantic content predicates rather than treating any change to a shared contract file as relevant. Negative controls prove unrelated flag/tool-schema edits stay inactive while --full-history changes activate the annotation set. The focused gate passed 16/16, the real diff reports zero active sets, token baselines pass 79 surfaces, and full release verification passed 7,334 tests with exact 100/100/100/100 coverage."
  "2026-08-15T02:58:00.679Z","harness:codex","Review reliability evidence 2026-08-15: exact coverage showed the two real-worktree semantic-trigger controls take 26-55 seconds under the fully parallel 500-file run although they finish in 7-10 seconds alone. Their test-only timeout is now 120 seconds; no gate threshold, trigger predicate, assertion, or fail-closed behavior changed. The focused 16-test suite and exact 7,337-test coverage pass."
  "2026-08-15T03:01:45.000Z","harness:codex","Final review evidence: linked surface-replication contracts passed 16/16 tests with unchanged gate thresholds and bounded 120-second test harness timeouts."
  "2026-08-17T09:12:35.696Z","harness:codex","Recurrence evidence 2026-08-17: PR #1053 exact head 7f94e0001 added an authoritative non-SQLite history fallback in src/core/history/event-index.ts while leaving resolveDatabaseSync/setDatabaseSync unchanged. The database-sync-test-seam declaration still uses whole-file triggers, so hosted Gates (static) demanded an artificial edit to item-metadata-query-index.ts. Reusing this canonical content-scope item; no waiver and no unrelated production edit."
  "2026-08-17T09:15:17.334Z","harness:codex","TDD completion evidence 2026-08-17: the new database seam negative control failed against the whole-file declaration, proving unrelated queryHistoryEventStreams/readAuthoritativeHistoryEvents lines activated database-sync-test-seam. Both index triggers now match only load/resolve/runtime/set DatabaseSync seam markers. The focused gate passes 17/17; its positive control still requires the second member for a RuntimeDatabaseSync change; the real PR changeset reports active_sets=[]; defect-evidence passes."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-14T07:55:46.540Z","harness:codex","A file path is too coarse to be a replication trigger when one shared registry owns unrelated contracts. Content-scoped added/removed-line markers preserve fail-closed coupling without requiring artificial edits; absence of diff evidence must activate, not skip, the set."
